justification:
Pocan said the end of the eviction moratorium means "millions of Americans" could lose their housing in the middle of a pandemic." The U.S. Census Bureau’s weekly Household Pulse Survey found that 3,511,056 respondents are facing the "likelihood" of eviction in the next two months. Several media reports also noted that the threat of homelessness could impact millions as the U.S. Supreme Court ended the pandemic-related federal moratorium. However, there are a few states that have implemented eviction moratoriums at the state level. Wisconsin is not one of those  states. For a statement that is accurate and there’s nothing significant missing, our rating is .   window.gciAnalyticsUAID = 'PMJS-TEALIUM-COBRAND';
