Fitzgerald said Wisconsin has "no tracing program going on that we can speak of." Wisconsin — like every other state — is still ramping up the capacity for tracing. And there have clearly been gaps in the work so far. But it’s a significant exaggeration to summarize that as having no program when hundreds of people are doing this work around the state. Tracing was being done around the state when Fitzgerald said this, and those efforts have continued to ramp up since.  We rate this  . window.gciAnalyticsUAID = 'PMJS-TEALIUM-COBRAND';
