In his endorsement video for Sanders, Pocan said that people in 1990 were making the same amount per hour as he saw advertised for the Amazon distribution center in Kenosha today. A quick comparison shows that wages today are slightly higher than what they were then, once inflation is factored in.   But the cost of everyday goods like rent, groceries and cars have outpaced that median wage growth, meaning a worker’s 1990 weekly paycheck, at a $10.43-an-hour rate, would have held more spending power than the $23.33-an-hour rate does today. We rate Pocan’s  .   window.gciAnalyticsUAID = 'PMJS-TEALIUM-COBRAND';
